IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc16-dna-definitions`

-- ccc16-open-court.l4 -- sections 486 to 486.31, 486.7 and 486.71 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XV): exclusion of the public, support persons and animals,
-- testimony outside the court room, the accused not to cross-examine a witness, non-disclosure of a witness's identity, security of witnesses.
-- Part agent ccc16. Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Imports the keel's core, and ccc16-dna-definitions for the row type and the matcher of a list of offence provisions
-- (`s 487.04 listed provision`, `s 487.04 the provision is on the list`): a rule stated once.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- Conventions taken here (each in NOTES.md, fork register and marginal readings):
--   * a power named "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12); who may apply is a limit of the grant: another applicant answers NOTHING;
--   * a duty ("shall") answers JUST FALSE where its trigger ("on application", "If ... is not made", "If the judge ... does not make an order") fails, or where its "unless" is met
--     (case by case, the maintainer, 2026-11-05); where the witness or offence is outside the class the subsection speaks of, NOTHING (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05: a scope limit with no "only");
--   * the same words recur in several sections (the place where the application is made, the factors, "No adverse inference", "Written reasons", "Inquiry by court"): each subsection has its own
--     function, generated from the same pattern so that they cannot drift apart.
-- The terms of section 2 the text uses ("victim", "intimate partner", "justice system participant") are asked as facts (MAYBE BOOLEAN where the keel's function can answer NOTHING).

§ `The applicant: shared type`

-- Who asks the judge or justice for an order. The text names the prosecutor and a witness (and, in section 486 and 486.7, the judge or justice on their own motion); the accused is named as an applicant only in section 486(3).
DECLARE `s 486 who applies for the order` IS ONE OF
    `s 486 the prosecutor`
    `s 486 a witness`
    `s 486 the judge or justice on their own motion`
    `s 486 the accused`
    `s 486 another person`

§ `Section 486 -- Exclusion of public`

-- 486(1) Any proceedings against an accused shall be held in open court, but ...
-- src:8765 | 486 (1) Any proceedings against an accused shall be held in open court, but the presiding judge or justice may, on application of the prosecutor or a witness or on his or her own motion, order the exclusion of all or any members of the public from the court room for all or part of the proceedings, or order that the witness testify behind a screen or other device that would allow the witness not to be seen by members of the public, if the judge or justice is of the opinion that such an order is in the interest of public morals, the maintenance of order or the proper administration of justice or is necessary to prevent injury to international relations or national defence or national security.
@ref s 486(1) (open court) (src:8765)
GIVEN `an order has been made under subsection 486(1) excluding the public, or that the witness testify behind a screen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486(1) the proceedings against the accused are held in open court` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an order has been made under subsection 486(1) excluding the public, or that the witness testify behind a screen`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "but the presiding judge or justice may, on application of the prosecutor or a witness or on his or her own motion, order the exclusion of all or any members of the public from the court room"

DECLARE `s 486(1) the order sought` IS ONE OF
    `s 486(1) the exclusion of all or any members of the public from the court room for all or part of the proceedings`
    `s 486(1) that the witness testify behind a screen or other device that would allow the witness not to be seen by members of the public`
    `s 486(1) an order of another kind`

-- "... the presiding judge or justice may, on application of the prosecutor or a witness or on his or her own motion, order ... if the judge or justice is of the opinion that such an order is in the interest of public
-- morals, the maintenance of order or the proper administration of justice or is necessary to prevent injury to international relations or national defence or national security."
-- src:8765 | 486 (1) Any proceedings against an accused shall be held in open court, but the presiding judge or justice may, on application of the prosecutor or a witness or on his or her own motion, order the exclusion of all or any members of the public from the court room for all or part of the proceedings, or order that the witness testify behind a screen or other device that would allow the witness not to be seen by members of the public, if the judge or justice is of the opinion that such an order is in the interest of public morals, the maintenance of order or the proper administration of justice or is necessary to prevent injury to international relations or national defence or national security.
@ref s 486(1) (the power) (src:8765)
GIVEN `who seeks the order` IS A `s 486 who applies for the order`
      `the order sought` IS A `s 486(1) the order sought`
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of public morals, the maintenance of order or the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is necessary to prevent injury to international relations or national defence or national security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486(1) the presiding judge or justice may order the exclusion of the public or that the witness testify behind a screen` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((`who seeks the order` EQUALS `s 486 the accused`) OR (`who seeks the order` EQUALS `s 486 another person`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on application of the prosecutor or a witness or on his or her own motion"
        IF (`the order sought` EQUALS `s 486(1) an order of another kind`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "order the exclusion of all or any members of the public from the court room for all or part of the proceedings, or order that the witness testify behind a screen or other device"
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of public morals, the maintenance of order or the proper administration of justice` OR `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is necessary to prevent injury to international relations or national defence or national security` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge or justice is of the opinion that such an order is in the interest of public morals, the maintenance of order or the proper administration of justice"

-- 486(1.1) Application: where and when the application may be made (the same words recur in 486.1(2.1), 486.2(2.1), 486.3(4.1) and 486.7(2)).
-- src:8767 | (1.1) The application may be made, during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice or, before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings or, if that judge or justice has not been determined, to any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place.
@ref s 486(1.1) (the places the application may be made) (src:8767)
DECLARE `s 486(1.1) when the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings`
    `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin`

DECLARE `s 486(1.1) to whom the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice`
    `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings`
    `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place`
    `s 486(1.1) another judge or justice`

-- src:8767 | (1.1) The application may be made, during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice or, before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings or, if that judge or justice has not been determined, to any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place.
@ref s 486(1.1) (src:8767)
GIVEN `when the application is made` IS A `s 486(1.1) when the application is made`
      `to whom the application is made` IS A `s 486(1.1) to whom the application is made`
      `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486(1.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `when the application is made`
    WHEN `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` THEN
        CONSIDER `to whom the application is made`
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice"
    WHEN `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` THEN
        CONSIDER `to whom the application is made`
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` THEN
            IF `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings"
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` THEN
            IF `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if that judge or justice has not been determined, to any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place"
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings"


-- 486(2) Factors to be considered
-- src:8769 | (2) In determining whether the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice, the judge or justice shall consider
-- src:8770 | (a) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process;
-- src:8771 | (b) the safeguarding of the interests of witnesses under the age of 18 years in all proceedings;
-- src:8772 | (c) the ability of the witness to give a full and candid account of the acts complained of if the order were not made;
-- src:8773 | (d) whether the witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation;
-- src:8774 | (e) the protection of justice system participants who are involved in the proceedings;
-- src:8775 | (f) whether effective alternatives to the making of the proposed order are available in the circumstances;
-- src:8776 | (g) the salutary and deleterious effects of the proposed order; and
-- src:8777 | (h) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant.
@ref s 486(2) (the lead-in and factors) (src:8769-8777)
DECLARE `s 486(2) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 486(2)(a) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process`
    `s 486(2)(b) the safeguarding of the interests of witnesses under the age of 18 years in all proceedings`
    `s 486(2)(c) the ability of the witness to give a full and candid account of the acts complained of if the order were not made`
    `s 486(2)(d) whether the witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation`
    `s 486(2)(e) the protection of justice system participants who are involved in the proceedings`
    `s 486(2)(f) whether effective alternatives to the making of the proposed order are available in the circumstances`
    `s 486(2)(g) the salutary and deleterious effects of the proposed order`
    `s 486(2)(h) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`

@ref s 486(2) (src:8769-8777)
GIVEN f IS A `s 486(2) factor`
      `the judge or justice is determining whether the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice considers the factor relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486(2) the judge or justice must consider the factor` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the judge or justice is determining whether the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining whether the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice"
    ELSE CONSIDER f
         WHEN `s 486(2)(h) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant` THEN
             IF `the judge or justice considers the factor relevant`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


-- 486(3) If an accused is charged with an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3) or section 163.1, 170, ..., 286.2 or 286.3 and the prosecutor or the accused applies for an
