-- src:8779 | (3) If an accused is charged with an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3) or section 163.1, 170, 171, 171.1, 172, 172.1, 172.2, 173, 271, 272, 273, 279.01, 279.011, 279.02, 279.03, 286.1, 286.2 or 286.3 and the prosecutor or the accused applies for an order under subsection (1), the judge or justice shall, if no such order is made, state, by reference to the circumstances of the case, the reason for not making an order.
@ref s 486(3) (src:8779)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `who applies for an order under subsection (1)` IS A `s 486 who applies for the order`
      `no such order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`s 487.04 the provision is on the list` `the offence charged` `s 486(3) the listed offences`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an accused is charged with an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155"
        IF (NOT ((`who applies for an order under subsection (1)` EQUALS `s 486 the prosecutor`) OR (`who applies for an order under subsection (1)` EQUALS `s 486 the accused`))) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the prosecutor or the accused applies for an order under subsection (1)"
        IF (NOT `no such order is made`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if no such order is made"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8781 | (4) No adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section.
@ref s 486(4) (src:8781)
GIVEN `the inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486(4) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` MEANS
    IF `the inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of an inference from that fact


§ `Section 486.1 -- Support person or animal -- witnesses under 18 or who have a disability`

-- 486.1(1) the judge or justice shall, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is under the age of 18 years or who has a mental or physical disability, or on application of such
-- a witness, order that a support person of the witness's choice or a support animal be permitted to be present and to be close to the witness while the witness testifies, unless ... would interfere with the proper administration of justice.
-- src:8783 | 486.1 (1) In any proceedings against an accused, the judge or justice shall, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is under the age of 18 years or who has a mental or physical disability, or on application of such a witness, order that a support person of the witness’s choice or a support animal be permitted to be present and to be close to the witness while the witness testifies, unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 486.1(1) (src:8783)
GIVEN `who applies for the order` IS A `s 486 who applies for the order`
      `the age of the witness, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the witness has a mental or physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.1(1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT ((`the age of the witness, in years` LESS THAN 18) OR `the witness has a mental or physical disability`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a witness who is under the age of 18 years or who has a mental or physical disability"
        IF (NOT ((`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 the prosecutor`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 a witness`))) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is under the age of 18 years or who has a mental or physical disability, or on application of such a witness"
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 486.1(1.1) Victims -- certain offences: an offence that is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose, an offence related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons or an offence committed
-- against their intimate partner. The same words recur in 486.2(1.1) and 486.3(2), which call this helper.
-- src:8785 | (1.1) In any proceedings against an accused in respect of an offence that is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose, an offence related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons or an offence committed against their intimate partner, the judge or justice shall, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is a victim, or on application of such a witness, order that a support person of the witness’s choice or a support animal be permitted to be present and to be close to the witness while the witness testifies, unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 486.1(1.1) (the offences) (src:8785)
GIVEN `the offence is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 intimate partner: the offence is committed against the accused's intimate partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 486.1(1.1) the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` MEANS
       `the offence is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose`
    OR `the offence is related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons`
    OR (`s 2 intimate partner: the offence is committed against the accused's intimate partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

-- src:8785 | (1.1) In any proceedings against an accused in respect of an offence that is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose, an offence related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons or an offence committed against their intimate partner, the judge or justice shall, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is a victim, or on application of such a witness, order that a support person of the witness’s choice or a support animal be permitted to be present and to be close to the witness while the witness testifies, unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 486.1(1.1) (src:8785)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 victim: the witness is a victim` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `who applies for the order` IS A `s 486 who applies for the order`
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.1(1.1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for a victim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` AND (`s 2 victim: the witness is a victim` EQUALS JUST TRUE))) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an offence that is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose, an offence related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons or an offence committed against their intimate partner"
        IF (NOT ((`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 the prosecutor`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 a witness`))) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is a victim, or on application of such a witness"
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8787 | (1.2) If an application for an order under subsection (1) or (1.1) is not made, the judge or justice shall inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to inform the witness that such an application may be made.
@ref s 486.1(1.2) (src:8787)
GIVEN `an application for an order under subsection (1) or (1.1) is not made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.1(1.2) the judge or justice must inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to inform the witness that an application may be made` MEANS
    IF `an application for an order under subsection (1) or (1.1) is not made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application for an order under subsection (1) or (1.1) is not made"


-- 486.1(2) Other witnesses: the judge or justice may, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness, or on application of a witness, order a support person or animal if of the opinion that the order
-- would facilitate the giving of a full and candid account by the witness of the acts complained of or would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice.
-- src:8789 | (2) In any proceedings against an accused, the judge or justice may, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness, or on application of a witness, order that a support person of the witness’s choice or a support animal be permitted to be present and to be close to the witness while the witness testifies if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would facilitate the giving of a full and candid account by the witness of the acts complained of or would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 486.1(2) (src:8789)
GIVEN `who applies for the order` IS A `s 486 who applies for the order`
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would facilitate the giving of a full and candid account by the witness of the acts complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.1(2) the judge or justice may order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for another witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT ((`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 the prosecutor`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 a witness`))) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness, or on application of a witness"
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would facilitate the giving of a full and candid account by the witness of the acts complained of` OR `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would facilitate the giving of a full and candid account by the witness of the acts complained of or would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice"

-- src:8791 | (2.1) An application may be made, during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice or, before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings or, if that judge or justice has not been determined, to any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place.
@ref s 486.1(2.1) (src:8791)
GIVEN `when the application is made` IS A `s 486(1.1) when the application is made`
      `to whom the application is made` IS A `s 486(1.1) to whom the application is made`
      `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.1(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `when the application is made`
    WHEN `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` THEN
        CONSIDER `to whom the application is made`
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice"
    WHEN `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` THEN
        CONSIDER `to whom the application is made`
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` THEN
            IF `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings"
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` THEN
            IF `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if that judge or justice has not been determined, to any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place"
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings"


-- src:8793 | (3) In determining whether to make an order under subsection (2), the judge or justice shall consider
-- src:8794 | (a) the age of the witness;
-- src:8795 | (b) the witness’ mental or physical disabilities, if any;
-- src:8796 | (c) the nature of the offence;
-- src:8797 | (d) the nature of any relationship between the witness and the accused;
-- src:8798 | (e) whether the witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation;
-- src:8799 | (f) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process; and
-- src:8800 | (g) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant.
@ref s 486.1(3) (the lead-in and factors) (src:8793-8800)
DECLARE `s 486.1(3) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 486.1(3)(a) the age of the witness`
    `s 486.1(3)(b) the witness’ mental or physical disabilities, if any`
    `s 486.1(3)(c) the nature of the offence`
    `s 486.1(3)(d) the nature of any relationship between the witness and the accused`
    `s 486.1(3)(e) whether the witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation`
    `s 486.1(3)(f) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process`
    `s 486.1(3)(g) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`

@ref s 486.1(3) (src:8793-8800)
GIVEN f IS A `s 486.1(3) factor`
      `the judge or justice is determining whether to make an order under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice considers the factor relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.1(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the judge or justice is determining whether to make an order under subsection (2)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining whether to make an order under subsection (2)"
    ELSE CONSIDER f
         WHEN `s 486.1(3)(g) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant` THEN
             IF `the judge or justice considers the factor relevant`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


-- 486.1(4) The judge or justice shall not permit a witness to be a support person unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that doing so is necessary for the proper administration of justice.
-- The answer is the bar: JUST TRUE where a witness would be a support person and the judge or justice is not of that opinion.
-- src:8801 | Witness not to be a support person
-- src:8802 | (4) The judge or justice shall not permit a witness to be a support person unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that doing so is necessary for the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 486.1(4) (src:8801-8802)
GIVEN `the proposed support person is a witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that permitting the witness to be a support person is necessary for the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.1(4) the judge or justice is barred from permitting a witness to be a support person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the proposed support person is a witness`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a witness as support person
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that permitting the witness to be a support person is necessary for the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that doing so is necessary for the proper administration of justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 486.1(5) The judge or justice may order that the support person and the witness not communicate with each other while the witness testifies.
