    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge or justice does not make an order under this section"


§ `Section 486.2 -- Testimony outside court room -- witnesses under 18 or who have a disability`

-- 486.2(1) Despite section 650 ... shall, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is under the age of 18 years or who is able to communicate evidence but may have difficulty doing so by reason of a
-- mental or physical disability, or on application of such a witness, order that the witness testify, at the option of the witness, either outside the court room or behind a screen or other device that would allow the
-- witness not to see the accused, unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice.
-- src:8810 | 486.2 (1) Despite section 650, in any proceedings against an accused, the judge or justice shall, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is under the age of 18 years or who is able to communicate evidence but may have difficulty doing so by reason of a mental or physical disability, or on application of such a witness, order that the witness testify, at the option of the witness, either outside the court room or behind a screen or other device that would allow the witness not to see the accused, unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 486.2(1) (src:8810)
GIVEN `who applies for the order` IS A `s 486 who applies for the order`
      `the age of the witness, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the witness is able to communicate evidence but may have difficulty doing so by reason of a mental or physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.2(1) the judge or justice must order that the witness testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT ((`the age of the witness, in years` LESS THAN 18) OR `the witness is able to communicate evidence but may have difficulty doing so by reason of a mental or physical disability`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a witness who is under the age of 18 years or who is able to communicate evidence but may have difficulty doing so by reason of a mental or physical disability"
        IF (NOT ((`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 the prosecutor`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 a witness`))) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is under the age of 18 years or who is able to communicate evidence but may have difficulty doing so by reason of a mental or physical disability, or on application of such a witness"
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 486.2(1.1) Victims -- certain offences (the offence kinds are those of 486.1(1.1)).
-- src:8812 | (1.1) Despite section 650, in any proceedings against an accused in respect of an offence that is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose, an offence related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons or an offence committed against their intimate partner, the judge or justice shall, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is a victim, or on application of such a witness, order that the witness testify, at the option of the witness, either outside the court room or behind a screen or other device that would allow the witness not to see the accused, unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 486.2(1.1) (src:8812)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 victim: the witness is a victim` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `who applies for the order` IS A `s 486 who applies for the order`
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.2(1.1) the judge or justice must order that the victim testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` AND (`s 2 victim: the witness is a victim` EQUALS JUST TRUE))) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an offence that is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose, an offence related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons or an offence committed against their intimate partner"
        IF (NOT ((`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 the prosecutor`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 a witness`))) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is a victim, or on application of such a witness"
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

