§ `Section 486.3 -- Accused not to cross-examine witness under 18`

-- 486.3(1) the judge or justice shall, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is under the age of 18 years, or on application of such a witness, order that the accused not personally
-- cross-examine the witness, unless ... the proper administration of justice requires the accused to personally conduct the cross-examination. If such an order is made, the judge or justice shall appoint counsel.
-- src:8839 | 486.3 (1) In any proceedings against an accused, the judge or justice shall, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is under the age of 18 years, or on application of such a witness, order that the accused not personally cross-examine the witness, unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the proper administration of justice requires the accused to personally conduct the cross-examination. If such an order is made, the judge or justice shall appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination.
@ref s 486.3(1) (the order) (src:8839)
GIVEN `who applies for the order` IS A `s 486 who applies for the order`
      `the age of the witness, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the proper administration of justice requires the accused to personally conduct the cross-examination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.3(1) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the witness under 18` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the age of the witness, in years` LESS THAN 18)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a witness who is under the age of 18 years"
        IF (NOT ((`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 the prosecutor`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 a witness`))) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is under the age of 18 years, or on application of such a witness"
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the proper administration of justice requires the accused to personally conduct the cross-examination` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the proper administration of justice requires the accused to personally conduct the cross-examination"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8839 | 486.3 (1) In any proceedings against an accused, the judge or justice shall, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is under the age of 18 years, or on application of such a witness, order that the accused not personally cross-examine the witness, unless the judge or justice is of the opinion that the proper administration of justice requires the accused to personally conduct the cross-examination. If such an order is made, the judge or justice shall appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination.
@ref s 486.3(1) (counsel) (src:8839)
GIVEN `the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.3(1) the judge or justice must appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination` MEANS
    IF `the order is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If such an order is made, the judge or justice shall appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination"

