GIVEN `the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.3(2) the judge or justice must appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination` MEANS
    IF `the order is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If such an order is made, the judge or justice shall appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination"

-- src:8843 | (2.1) If an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2) is not made, the judge or justice shall inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to inform the witness that such an application may be made.
@ref s 486.3(2.1) (src:8843)
GIVEN `an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2) is not made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.3(2.1) the judge or justice must inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to inform the witness that an application may be made` MEANS
    IF `an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2) is not made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2) is not made"


-- 486.3(3) the judge or justice may, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is not entitled to make an application under subsection (1) or (2), or on application of such a witness, order that
-- the accused not personally cross-examine the witness if ... would allow the giving of a full and candid account ... or would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice.
-- src:8845 | (3) In any proceedings against an accused, the judge or justice may, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is not entitled to make an application under subsection (1) or (2), or on application of such a witness, order that the accused not personally cross-examine the witness if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would allow the giving of a full and candid account from the witness of the acts complained of or would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice. If the order is made, the judge or justice shall appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination.
@ref s 486.3(3) (the order) (src:8845)
GIVEN `who applies for the order` IS A `s 486 who applies for the order`
      `the witness is not entitled to make an application under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would allow the giving of a full and candid account from the witness of the acts complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.3(3) the judge or justice may order that the accused not personally cross-examine another witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the witness is not entitled to make an application under subsection (1) or (2)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a witness who is not entitled to make an application under subsection (1) or (2)"
        IF (NOT ((`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 the prosecutor`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486 a witness`))) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is not entitled to make an application under subsection (1) or (2), or on application of such a witness"
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would allow the giving of a full and candid account from the witness of the acts complained of` OR `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would allow the giving of a full and candid account from the witness of the acts complained of or would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice"

-- src:8845 | (3) In any proceedings against an accused, the judge or justice may, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a witness who is not entitled to make an application under subsection (1) or (2), or on application of such a witness, order that the accused not personally cross-examine the witness if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order would allow the giving of a full and candid account from the witness of the acts complained of or would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice. If the order is made, the judge or justice shall appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination.
@ref s 486.3(3) (counsel) (src:8845)
GIVEN `the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.3(3) the judge or justice must appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination` MEANS
    IF `the order is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the order is made, the judge or justice shall appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination"

-- src:8847 | (4) In determining whether to make an order under subsection (3), the judge or justice shall consider
-- src:8848 | (a) the age of the witness;
-- src:8849 | (b) the witness’ mental or physical disabilities, if any;
-- src:8850 | (c) the nature of the offence;
-- src:8851 | (d) whether the witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation;
-- src:8852 | (e) the nature of any relationship between the witness and the accused;
-- src:8853 | (f) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process; and
-- src:8854 | (g) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant.
@ref s 486.3(4) (the lead-in and factors) (src:8847-8854)
DECLARE `s 486.3(4) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 486.3(4)(a) the age of the witness`
    `s 486.3(4)(b) the witness’ mental or physical disabilities, if any`
    `s 486.3(4)(c) the nature of the offence`
    `s 486.3(4)(d) whether the witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation`
    `s 486.3(4)(e) the nature of any relationship between the witness and the accused`
    `s 486.3(4)(f) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process`
    `s 486.3(4)(g) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`

@ref s 486.3(4) (src:8847-8854)
GIVEN f IS A `s 486.3(4) factor`
      `the judge or justice is determining whether to make an order under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice considers the factor relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.3(4) the judge or justice must consider the factor` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the judge or justice is determining whether to make an order under subsection (3)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining whether to make an order under subsection (3)"
    ELSE CONSIDER f
         WHEN `s 486.3(4)(g) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant` THEN
             IF `the judge or justice considers the factor relevant`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


-- src:8856 | (4.1) An application referred to in any of subsections (1) to (3) may be made during the proceedings to the presiding judge or justice or, before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings or, if that judge or justice has not been determined, to any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place.
@ref s 486.3(4.1) (src:8856)
GIVEN `when the application is made` IS A `s 486(1.1) when the application is made`
      `to whom the application is made` IS A `s 486(1.1) to whom the application is made`
      `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.3(4.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `when the application is made`
    WHEN `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` THEN
        CONSIDER `to whom the application is made`
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice"
    WHEN `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` THEN
        CONSIDER `to whom the application is made`
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` THEN
            IF `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings"
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` THEN
            IF `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if that judge or justice has not been determined, to any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place"
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings"

