§ `Section 486.7 -- Security of witnesses`

-- 486.7(1) the presiding judge or justice may, on application of the prosecutor or a witness or on his or her own motion, make any order, other than one that may be made under any of sections 486 to 486.5,
-- if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is necessary to protect the security of any witness and is otherwise in the interest of the proper administration of justice.
-- "(other than X)" is one of the maintainer's case-by-case sites: an order that may be made under sections 486 to 486.5 is outside this power and answers JUST FALSE.
-- src:8993 | 486.7 (1) In any proceedings against an accused, the presiding judge or justice may, on application of the prosecutor or a witness or on his or her own motion, make any order, other than one that may be made under any of sections 486 to 486.5, if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is necessary to protect the security of any witness and is otherwise in the interest of the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 486.7(1) (src:8993)
GIVEN `who seeks the order` IS A `s 486 who applies for the order`
      `the order is one that may be made under any of sections 486 to 486.5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is necessary to protect the security of any witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is otherwise in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.7(1) the presiding judge or justice may make an order to protect the security of a witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((`who seeks the order` EQUALS `s 486 the accused`) OR (`who seeks the order` EQUALS `s 486 another person`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on application of the prosecutor or a witness or on his or her own motion"
        IF `the order is one that may be made under any of sections 486 to 486.5` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "make any order, other than one that may be made under any of sections 486 to 486.5"
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is necessary to protect the security of any witness` AND `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is otherwise in the interest of the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is necessary to protect the security of any witness and is otherwise in the interest of the proper administration of justice"

-- src:8995 | (2) The application may be made, during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice or, before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings or, if that judge or justice has not been determined, to any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place.
@ref s 486.7(2) (src:8995)
GIVEN `when the application is made` IS A `s 486(1.1) when the application is made`
      `to whom the application is made` IS A `s 486(1.1) to whom the application is made`
      `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.7(2) the application may be made to the judge or justice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `when the application is made`
    WHEN `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` THEN
        CONSIDER `to whom the application is made`
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice"
    WHEN `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` THEN
        CONSIDER `to whom the application is made`
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` THEN
            IF `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings"
        WHEN `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` THEN
            IF `the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings has been determined`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if that judge or justice has not been determined, to any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place"
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings"

