§ `Section 486.71 -- For greater certainty`

-- 486.71 For greater certainty, nothing in sections 486 to 486.5 or 486.7 prohibits a judge or justice from making more than one order regarding the same witness under those sections.
-- src:9012 | 486.71 For greater certainty, nothing in sections 486 to 486.5 or 486.7 prohibits a judge or justice from making more than one order regarding the same witness under those sections.
@ref s 486.71 (src:9012)
GIVEN `the orders are made under those sections regarding the same witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.71 the judge or justice is prohibited from making more than one order regarding the same witness` MEANS
    IF `the orders are made under those sections regarding the same witness`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in sections 486 to 486.5 or 486.7 prohibits a judge or justice from making more than one order regarding the same witness under those sections"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "regarding the same witness under those sections"
